{
  "summary": "Enables `-Wunused` and related compiler warning flags in CMake, resolving existing unused variable and parameter warnings across the repository. It drops or comments out unused parameter names, adds `[[maybe_unused]]` attributes, refactors several RPC method implementations to use the `Arg<>()` helper, and includes temporary changes for vendored subtree dependencies.",
  "problem": "The build system does not enable `-Wunused`, allowing unused code, variables, and parameters to silently accumulate across the codebase. This omission can conceal subtle programming errors where code or parameters were accidentally forgotten rather than intentionally omitted.",
  "evidence": [
    "The PR description points to a recent case (#36137) of 'what was thought to be dead code, but it'd actually just been forgotten to be used'.",
    "The author links eight dead code removal PRs merged within the preceding two months (#35679, #35910, #35914, #35971, #36009, #36012, #36103, #36127) as evidence of churn that compiler warnings would prevent."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Contains three `[[nomerge]]` commits with fixes intended for external subtrees (minisketch, leveldb, and libmultiprocess). It also bundles an RPC argument lookup change in `GetParamIndex` alongside mechanical parameter silencing across 160 files.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased to reflect several intervening PR merges (including #36275 and #36509), reducing the file touch count from 171 to 160.",
  "card": "Enables `-Wunused` compiler flags in CMake and silences existing warnings across 160 files by omitting unused parameter names, adding `[[maybe_unused]]`, and refactoring RPC argument helpers. Without warning enforcement, dead code accumulates and can mask logic bugs where intended variable or parameter usage was forgotten (as observed in #36137). Merging is blocked on upstream subtree PRs in Minisketch and libmultiprocess.",
